From 2697f74352f5cec53c52ac41ec39fdde16e9b7b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:13:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Keep a lost incarnation refused until a MAP of it
 verifies

Codex's review of the previous commit: a MAP of the same
MappingInternal replaced the lost entry with a fresh pending one before
checking it, and the guard refused only lost or condemned entries. So a
MAP whose check could not be read, or whose two reads disagreed, left a
pending entry the guard let writes through; and one that failed its
check (class, layout, a count at zero at MAP) removed the entry, and an
unwatched mapping is unrefused too.

The refusal is now a latch, Watched::unowned, set where the chain is
lost and carried by a MAP of the same MappingInternal into its fresh
entry. The guard refuses every write while it is set, in any phase. It
is lifted only where that MAP's check passes: the whole chain,
MappingInternal to IOSurface to both descriptors, read alike twice, and
both counts positive, which a check made later than the MAP must show
as well (OFF wire_guard_unowned_cleared ... reason=verified_map
at=map|late surface_wire= table_wire=). Otherwise it stays:

- not readable, or the two reads disagree: the entry stays pending and
  refused, and is checked again at the next sample;
- the check fails: the entry is not removed but goes back to lost, not
  sampled and refused, until a later MAP verifies.

Each is said at the MAP: OFF wire_guard_unowned_kept mapping= internal=
lost= why=not_yet|inconclusive:<link>|<check reason>|wire_not_positive
at=map. A condemned incarnation is still not cleared by a MAP of the
same MappingInternal, and a lost one is no evidence for a mapping the
surface quarantine would free. Phase::Lost now only means not sampled;
the reason lives in the latch.

Tests (lib, --test-threads=1): 2322 passed, 1 failed: the cursor test,
which reads vendor/qemu/ui/cursor.c, absent from this worktree.
runtime::mapper::wire_watch: 39 passed, 5 of them new, each on 13.6
with mapping 2 lost and made again where it was. A MAP that cannot be
read, one whose two reads disagree (and a write whose own check
disagrees too), one whose IOSurface is 14.6.1's class, and one whose
surface count reads 0 all keep its writes refused, and each is then
lifted by a check that verifies. A MAP that verifies gives the writes
back. The previous commit's lost test now expects reason=verified_map
at=map. With the latch not carried across the MAP, the four refusal
tests and that lost test fail, and the verified MAP still passes
(checked).

